05;214;244m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249msrc/server.js\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m matches the exact URL        \r\n  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m/products\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m and returns an empty 404 for everything else. That is why \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m/products/42\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m fails, and \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m/products/1\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m fails too.    \r\n  Details are in \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdiscover.md\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m.                                                                                           \r\n                                                                                                                        \r\n  \u001b[1mSpec (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mspec.md\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m):\u001b[22m                                                                                                       \r\n  - \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[22m Add \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mGET /products/:id\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m. A known id returns 200 with the product as JSON. An unknown or non-numeric id returns   \r\n    404 with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m{\"error\":\"not found\"}\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m and \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcontent-type: application/json\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m.                                                  \r\n  - \u001b[1mUnchanged:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mGET /products\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m keeps working.                                                                             \r\n  - \u001b[1mTests:\u001b[22m Tests for the new behaviour are written first and fail before the change. The final criterion is that \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mnpm \u001b[38;2;205;214;244m   \r\n    \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mtest\u001b[38;2;205;214;244m passes.                                                                                                        \r\n  - \u001b[1mAssumption (AC-6):\u001b[22m Other unmatched routes keep their empty 404. Tell me if you want them to return the JSON error as\r\n    well.                